## Original Content
Venture investors seem to be more upbeat than they have been in years about the future of fitness and wellness. Startup investment in those categories totaled more than $3.6 billion in the first half of this year, putting 2026 on pace to come in about a third higher than 2025.

## Summary
Venture investors are showing increased optimism in the fitness and wellness sector, with startup funding surpassing $3.6 billion in the first half of the year. This trend suggests that 2026 funding could be about a third higher than in 2025. Notably, investor interest is shifting towards AI and data technologies rather than traditional fitness equipment.

## Key Points
- Startup investment in fitness and wellness rebounded, totaling over $3.6 billion in the first half of the year.
- Funding for 2026 is on pace to be about a third higher than in 2025.
- Venture investors are more upbeat about the future of fitness and wellness than in previous years.
- Investor focus is shifting towards AI and data technologies instead of traditional fitness equipment like treadmills.


